# Meathook Massacre II, the other answers (CR 118.12, 119.4): cast for X = 2, each player sacrifices two creatures, all four deaths
# together, and four abilities trigger, one for each creature, none missed for the others dying at once. Bot1 sacrifices a Memnite
# and an Ornithopter and declines to pay for either, so both stay in its graveyard; Bot2 sacrifices a Memnite and an Ornithopter and
# pays 3 life for each, 14, so those stay in its graveyard and nothing comes back for Bot1. Bot1's own life stays 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Memnite
Ornithopter
Meathook Massacre II
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Meathook Massacre II.Cast(X: 2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Accept
Bot1.Decline
Bot1.Decline

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Battlefield = Meathook Massacre II; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Memnite; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Memnite
